      "side": 1,
      "message": "If I understand correctly, the EC is still supspended, but it is in the process of waking up. The ISH happens to be awake earlier, doesn\u0027t it?\nWhat happen if the EC goes to suspend, but the ISH is still up and send a message: the ISH will end up retrying CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_DSP_CLIENT_TX_RETRY_MAX times before giving up (150ms by default). Is it acceptable?\n\nShould power state transition be synchronized between ISH and EC via interrupt and acknowledgment messages?",
      "revId": "1be874cacc446ac6473429d1f47144b61e8de420",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "561f8f6f_f4f7c419",
